rectangle "nyx\n<size:16>[Software System]</size>" <<Boundary-bnl4>> {
  rectangle "nyx-engine\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library]</size>" <<Boundary-bnl4LWVuZ2luZQ==>> {
    rectangle "==Commands\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nThe Engine and its catalog: every action by name with JSON arguments, JSON Schema and JSON reply; the dispatcher; the guide cards a host reads on demand; the reductions of results (field handles, integrals, extrema, probes, overlaps). The window and the MCP server use the same entries." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.nyxengine.Commands
    rectangle "==Project\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nThe saved state: feature list, mesh settings, one ProblemSpec per physics, project materials. The format key is checked at the file boundary." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.nyxengine.Project
    rectangle "==Geometry operations\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nEvery edit of a geom feature list as a function that does it or says why not, and the descriptors of the geom operations (they live here because geom depends on serde only)." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.nyxengine.Geometryoperations
    rectangle "==Job runner and queue\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nMesh, solve, convergence and file jobs on their own threads with progress and cancel, queued in lanes (priority, owners in turn, stages shared by content), solves in a worker process (killed on cancel, its stage log mirrored, results read back from a file), memory estimates learned from the workers and admission by free memory, solving physics in the order of the one-way couplings (region names put into the scalars a kernel names by domain number), mesh convergence on a scratch engine with solutions compared by index, paired by nearest eigenvalue or one mode followed; the queue of the workspace as a folder run by a queue worker that outlives the window (ADR 95); warm starts between the points of a sweep (ADR 96)." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.nyxengine.Jobrunnerandqueue
    rectangle "==Command lists\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nA JSON-lines list of engine commands is parsed, checked against the catalog and its schemas, planned on a scratch engine (what would be meshed and solved, nothing run) and run in order through Engine::call." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.nyxengine.Commandlists
    rectangle "==API reference\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nOne Markdown page per engine command and an index, generated from Engine::catalog() (arguments flattened from the schema, an example that passes the check); docs/api is compared with it by a test." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.nyxengine.APIreference
    rectangle "==Meshing seam\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nMeshRequest to MeshedModel (mesh, names, label resolver); the only caller of the femcore mesher; absorbing layers across the two halves of a project; trial meshes and edit checks for the feedback while editing (ADR 92)." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.nyxengine.Meshingseam
    rectangle "==Materials\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nThe material library plus the materials a project carries, resolved at the study wavelength." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.nyxengine.Materials
    rectangle "==Analyses\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nRuns the analyses of nyx-analysis on the latest result of a physics." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.nyxengine.Analyses
    rectangle "==Results files\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nHDF5 results (serial or MPI-IO), the XDMF description, and opening a results file as a project with its results." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.nyxengine.Resultsfiles
    rectangle "==Store link\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nBinds the project to a workflow of the workspace, commits versions, records runs (card and metrics made here)." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.nyxengine.Storelink
    rectangle "==Registry and facade\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nThe physics compiled in (cargo features dfs, sms, ems) and the facade that re-exports what a front-end draws with." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.nyxengine.Registryandfacade
  }

  component "==geom\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library]</size>\n\nLean CSG-over-B-rep geometry kernel: feature lists, named regions and boundaries, selectors, exact projection oracles. Depends on serde and optional rayon only." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsTGlicmFyeQ==>> as nyx.geom
  database "==Project file\n<size:16>[Container: File .nyx.json]</size>\n\nEverything saved for one model: geometry, materials, boundary conditions, studies. JSON with a format key." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsU3RvcmU=>> as nyx.Projectfile
  database "==Results file\n<size:16>[Container: File .h5 and .xdmf]</size>\n\nProject, mesh and every solution of every solved physics, compressed, exact; with an XDMF description next to it." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsU3RvcmU=>> as nyx.Resultsfile
  database "==Material library\n<size:16>[Container: Files]</size>\n\nmaterials/*.toml next to the program: silicon, silica, sapphire, metals, nitrides, niobate and more, with sources." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsU3RvcmU=>> as nyx.Materiallibrary
  component "==nyx-physics\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library]</size>\n\nThe Physics trait, the problem envelope (ProblemSpec), descriptors, SolveResult, the registry type, validation, JSON Schemas." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsTGlicmFyeQ==>> as nyx.nyxphysics
  component "==nyx-dfs\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library]</size>\n\nDiffusion physics: heat and electrostatics. Typed problem, three-stage kernels, descriptors, goldens." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsTGlicmFyeSxLZXJuZWw=>> as nyx.nyxdfs
  component "==nyx-sms\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library]</size>\n\nSolid mechanics: static, eigenfrequency, PML, Floquet, low-reflecting boundaries, axisymmetric eigenfrequency study (bodies of revolution, axis conditions, cylindrical layers)." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsTGlicmFyeSxLZXJuZWw=>> as nyx.nyxsms
  component "==nyx-ems\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library]</size>\n\nEM waves: waveguide modes (real and complex), axisymmetric, cavity in 3D." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsTGlicmFyeSxLZXJuZWw=>> as nyx.nyxems
  component "==nyx-analysis\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library]</size>\n\nAnalyses of results: the polarization (Stokes parameters, Poincare sphere, classes, degenerate groups) as a function of a SolveResult and its mesh." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsTGlicmFyeQ==>> as nyx.nyxanalysis
  component "==nyx-store\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library]</size>\n\nWorkspace, workflow, experiment and run storage: manifests, append-only run log, versions, search, .nyx archives. Knows nothing of a project." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsTGlicmFyeQ==>> as nyx.nyxstore
  component "==femcore\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library]</size>\n\nThe FEM core: meshes, meshing and adaptation, linear algebra behind one driver, finite-element basics, the material specification and library, expressions." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsTGlicmFyeQ==>> as nyx.femcore
}

